            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary surgery in patients with poor ventricular function].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The surgical indication of coronary by-pass surgery in patients with bad ventricular function is difficult. We analysed retrospectively 87 patients operated on between February 1982 and November 1983. We show the benefit of this surgery even in patients without angina pectoris.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
